/-!
# The original nonsplit symplectic plane marking

The actor projection has kernel O2(L2), and the surjective binary natural-plane
map has the literal kernel C_V(L). Their intertwining equation uses original
ambient conjugation. Fixed lifting proves that O2(L2) centralizes the full
plane preimage. The actual commutator [V2,L2] is IrrPlus, maps onto the natural
plane, and is supplemented by the literal C_V(L). Its remaining quotient has
binary dimension at most the field degree. For field four this supplies the
repaired uniqueness application with only component membership explicit.
The full preimage is not asserted to be IrrPlus.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith I.2.3(1), 11.1.3 and 11.2.4, pp.413,765,769--770.
-/
